    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4623cd02",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: hillary_clinton_caught_telling_the_truth_april_fools; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts Hillary Clinton smiling and gesturing during a campaign event, overlaid with text that reads 'hillary clinton caught telling the truth!' and 'april fools!'. The overall intent is to create a humorous, satirical April Fools' joke by implying that Clinton was caught in a moment of truthfulness, which is then revealed as a prank. While the meme is not explicitly abusive, cyberbullying, or hateful, it is potentially harmful because it plays on public perceptions of political figures and can be interpreted as mocking or undermining their credibility. The juxtaposition of the image of a confident, charismatic politician with the text 'caught telling the truth' creates a comedic effect that relies on the audience's familiarity with political discourse and Clinton's public image. The 'April Fools!' tag clarifies the joke's nature, but the meme still risks being perceived as dismissive or sarcastic toward the subject, which can be seen as a form of political humor that may not be universally appreciated or may be interpreted as disrespectful in certain contexts. The meme does not contain any explicit toxic content such as racism, antisemitism, misogyny, or other forms of discrimination, but its potential to cause harm lies in its implication of dishonesty or exaggeration about a public figure, which could be seen as undermining trust in political discourse.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2be88f4a"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
